  "notes": "M7.5 is largest with P in 0-7200. R1 predicted 2281.5, onset measured by onsets/AIC at 2310 with huge STA/LTA ~267-416, physical P<S<R1 order. P predicted 908.3 but series 800-1000 is flat zero (find_peak=0); AIC in 908+-20 gives 890 snr 0, i.e. P below digitization threshold, reported as measured pick. Surface coda 2300-2870 is real M7.5; max by find_peak 2690-2870 is 2862 amp 2.2, preferred over larger -5.0 spike at 2563 which is a line-jump clip. 900-s duplication: 1892=2792-900, 1931~2831-900 (inside 2828-2842), 1427~2327-900 (R1 onset coda 2310-2331), all isolated 1-sample spikes on flat zero with low line_shift_similarity ~0.04-0.16, so early copies are wrong. 2534-2566 shows 1-spacing jumps -2 to -5 to -2 and flat segments, 3600-3782 flat -3 for ~180s, both non-physical helicorder jumps. Low-confidence spans 2828-2842 and 3798-4500 included as wrong."
